CAT = "auforkliftChecks"; SEG = "CHK"
Q = [
("When should a forklift pre-start check be done?",
 "Before use each shift", ["Once a week", "Only after lunch", "Once a month at servicing"],
 "Do the pre-start check before using the truck at the start of each shift, or as the manufacturer and site require. Weekly or monthly checks are servicing, not pre-starts."),
("During a pre-start you see paint cracking around a weld on the mast. What can this mean?",
 "Possible structural weakness", ["Normal wear that can be ignored", "Low hydraulic oil level", "Low tyre pressure"],
 "Paint separation and cracking around welds can mean the metal underneath is stressed or cracked. Tag the truck out and have it inspected."),
("During a pre-start you find a crack at the heel of a fork arm. What should you do?",
 "Tag it out and report it", ["Use it for light loads only", "Swap it with the other fork", "Weld it before the shift"],
 "A cracked fork arm can fail without warning under load. The truck must be taken out of service and the fork replaced or inspected by a competent person."),
("Why check the fork positioning pins or locks during a pre-start?",
 "So forks can't slide or shift", ["To set the load centre", "To adjust the angle of mast tilt", "To set the travel speed"],
 "The locks hold the forks in position on the carriage. An unlocked fork can slide sideways, unbalance the load or come off."),
("During a pre-start you find the data plate is missing. What should you do?",
 "Don't use it; report it", ["Use another truck's plate", "Judge capacity from its size", "Use it for light loads only"],
 "Without a legible data plate you cannot know the truck's rated capacity. Report it and do not use the truck until the correct plate is fitted."),
("What should you check on the tyres during a pre-start?",
 "Damage, wear and inflation", ["Only the front tyres", "Only the brand and the size marking", "Nothing on solid tyres"],
 "Check all tyres for cuts, chunks missing, wear and, on pneumatic tyres, correct inflation. Solid tyres still wear and get damaged."),
("A puddle of oil sits under the parked forklift at the pre-start. What should you do?",
 "Find the source and report it", ["Wipe it up and start work", "Top up the oil and start work", "Move the truck to a dry spot"],
 "A fluid leak can mean a failing hydraulic hose or seal, and the spill is a slip hazard. Find where it comes from and report it before use."),
("What should you check on the seatbelt during a pre-start?",
 "It latches and releases properly", ["It is tucked behind the seat", "It is left unclipped for quick exits", "It is only clean and dry"],
 "The seatbelt must be fitted, undamaged and working so it can hold you in the protective cab if the truck tips."),
("When should you adjust the seat and mirrors?",
 "Before moving off", ["While driving the aisle", "Only on long shifts", "After the first lift"],
 "Adjust the seat so you can reach every control and the mirrors so you can see, before the truck moves. Adjusting while driving takes your attention off the path."),
("During operational checks, how should you test the mast hydraulics?",
 "Run each function to full travel", ["Test lift with a full load", "Test lift but not tilt", "Leave it for the yearly service visit"],
 "Operate lift, lower, tilt and any side shift through their full range, checking they are smooth and controlled. A full-load test is not part of the operator's check."),
("What should you check on the brakes before starting work?",
 "Test service and park brakes", ["Only check the brake fluid colour", "Test them once a week", "Pump the pedal ten times"],
 "Test both the service brake and the park brake in a clear area before work. Brakes that are soft or pull must be reported."),
("During operational checks the steering has too much free play. What should you do?",
 "Report it and don't use it", ["Drive slowly for the shift", "Use it for empty runs only", "Tighten the column yourself"],
 "Steering faults can cause loss of control. Report the fault, tag the truck out and let a competent person repair it."),
("Which warning devices should you test during operational checks?",
 "Horn, beeper and lights", ["The horn only", "The lights, but only at night", "The beeper only"],
 "Test every warning device fitted, such as the horn, reversing beeper, flashing light and any blue spot. They warn people the truck is near."),
("While starting up you hear a grinding noise from the mast. What is the safe response?",
 "Shut down, tag out, report", ["Grease it and carry on", "Ignore it if it lifts", "Use it until the next service"],
 "Unusual noises are a sign of wear or damage. Stop, isolate the truck and report it so it can be checked."),
("On a battery-electric forklift, what should the pre-start include?",
 "Battery charge and cables", ["The engine oil level", "The radiator coolant level", "The LPG cylinder seal"],
 "Electric trucks need the battery charge, connector and cables checked, as the manufacturer requires. Oil, coolant and LPG checks are for engine-powered trucks."),
("On an LPG forklift, which of these is part of the pre-start?",
 "Engine oil and coolant levels", ["The charger plug and lead", "The traction battery's charge level", "Electrolyte in each cell"],
 "Engine trucks need fluid levels, fuel and the LPG cylinder fitting checked. Charger leads and traction battery cells belong to electric trucks."),
("When is the hydraulic oil level usually checked?",
 "With the mast fully lowered", ["With the forks fully raised", "With a load on the forks", "With the mast tilted forward"],
 "With the mast lowered the oil is back in the tank, giving a true reading. Follow the manufacturer's instructions for your truck."),
("Why check the truck's logbook at the start of a shift?",
 "To see past faults and repairs", ["To find the truck's rated capacity", "To log the load weights", "To set the travel speed"],
 "The logbook shows earlier faults, repairs and service dates, so you know the truck's history. Rated capacity is on the data plate."),
("A warning decal on the truck is faded and unreadable. What should you do?",
 "Report it to be replaced", ["Ignore it, it's cosmetic", "Peel it off completely", "Write over it in marker"],
 "Safety signs and labels must be visible and legible. Report damaged ones so the correct replacement is fitted."),
("The overhead guard has a bent bar. What should you do?",
 "Tag the truck out and report", ["Use it if the bend is only small", "Straighten it with a bar", "Drive with a hard hat on"],
 "The overhead guard protects you from falling loads. If it is damaged it may not hold, so the truck must not be used until it is assessed."),
("What should you look for on the mast lift chains?",
 "Even tension, wear and damage", ["Fresh paint on each link", "Slack on one side only", "Surface rust as a sign of strength"],
 "Chains should be evenly tensioned, lubricated as required and free of cracked, stiff or worn links. Uneven tension can tilt the carriage."),
("A fire extinguisher is fitted to the truck. What should you check?",
 "It is charged and secure", ["It is stored on the forks", "It is empty to save weight", "It is removed when driving"],
 "Check the extinguisher gauge, pin and mounting as part of the safety equipment check. It must be ready to use."),
("Why locate and test every control before moving the truck?",
 "To confirm each one works", ["To reset the hour meter", "To charge the battery", "To shorten the load centre"],
 "Controls differ between trucks. Identifying and testing each one before moving makes sure it works and that you know what it does."),
("Where should you do your pre-start and operational checks?",
 "On level ground clear of traffic", ["In a busy aisle to save time", "On a ramp so you can test the brakes", "Beside the loading dock edge"],
 "Checks need a safe, level area away from traffic, where the mast can be raised without striking anything."),
("How should you get on and off the forklift?",
 "Facing it, 3 points of contact", ["Jump down to save time", "Swing down on the steering wheel", "Step down onto the forks"],
 "Keep three points of contact, two hands and a foot or two feet and a hand, on the handholds and steps. Jumping causes many ankle and knee injuries."),
("Before you climb on, you see the step is greasy. What should you do?",
 "Clean it before getting on", ["Jump on to avoid the greasy step", "Step on the tyre instead", "Climb up using the mast"],
 "Steps and rungs must be free of grease, mud and other slip hazards before you access the truck."),
("Before starting the engine or switching on, what should you make sure of?",
 "Controls neutral, brake on", ["Forks raised a little off the floor", "Mast tilted forward", "Seatbelt unbuckled"],
 "Starting with the controls in neutral and the park brake on stops the truck or mast moving unexpectedly. Follow the manufacturer's start-up steps."),
("A jib attachment is fitted. What must your pre-start confirm?",
 "It is secured and rated", ["It matches the truck's colour", "It is held on with tape", "It needs no extra checks"],
 "An attachment must be securely fitted and have its own data plate, with the truck's capacity for that attachment shown. Check both before use."),
("Halfway through a shift the brakes start to feel soft. What should you do?",
 "Stop, park safely and report", ["Finish the shift, then report", "Pump the brakes and continue", "Drive slower for the shift"],
 "A defect found during work is treated like one found at pre-start. Stop, park safely, tag the truck out and report it."),
("Why record damage found during a pre-start?",
 "So it is tracked and repaired", ["So the truck can be re-rated", "So next shift can skip checks", "So the data plate can change"],
 "Recording damage creates a record that it was found, reported and fixed. It also tells the next operator about the truck's condition."),
("Why is an under-inflated tyre on one side a stability risk?",
 "The truck leans to that side", ["The truck goes faster", "The steering gets lighter", "The load centre gets shorter"],
 "Low pressure on one side tilts the truck and the mast, moving the centre of gravity toward that side. Pneumatic tyres must be at the pressure the manufacturer sets."),
("A hydraulic hose is weeping oil. Who should repair it?",
 "A competent person", ["The operator, with tape", "Any worker nearby", "The next operator on shift"],
 "Hydraulic systems hold high pressure, and repairs need the right parts and skills. Report it and leave the repair to an authorised, competent person."),
]
